# Reviewed and accepted findings for `trivy config`. One id per line, with the reason.
# Public web ports are the point of the service; SSH is restricted to admin_cidr.
AVD-AWS-0107
# Outbound is open on purpose: apt, Docker pulls, Let's Encrypt, DuckDNS. Restricting it is brittle.
AVD-AWS-0104
# Buckets use SSE-S3 (AES256). A customer-managed KMS key costs about $1/month per key and
# adds no protection against the threats here (no cross-account access, public access blocked).
AVD-AWS-0132
# The alerts topic carries only alarm names and states. CloudWatch cannot publish to a topic encrypted with the
# AWS-managed key (alias/aws/sns); that needs a customer-managed key (about $1/month), the same trade-off as AWS-0132.
AVD-AWS-0095
